show "=== Session contract: template ==="

remember a source called primary-source with "paste the verbatim source text here"
remember a claim called working-claim with "paste the claim text being verified here"

remember a string called source-state with "unscanned"
remember a string called claim-basis with "none"
remember a list called tracked-decisions with "none"
remember a list called open-questions with "none"
remember a number called decision-count with 0

remember how to disclose from status: show status
remember how to summarize from label: count label

when source-state is equal to "unscanned"
  show "HOLD: source not yet scanned — verify before consequential claims"

when claim-basis is equal to "inference" unless source-state is equal to "verified"
  show "WARNING: current claims are inferred, not verified against source"

when claim-basis is equal to "verified"
  show "OK: claims grounded in verified source"

show "--- state snapshot ---"
show source-state
show claim-basis
show tracked-decisions
show open-questions

show "--- example: citing the source before a consequential claim ---"
cite "paste" from primary-source

show "--- example: accumulating decisions and questions ---"
add "decision-architecture-three-layer" to tracked-decisions
add "decision-vocab-bounded-35" to tracked-decisions
add "question-pack-loader-design" to open-questions
show tracked-decisions
show open-questions
summarize from tracked-decisions

show "--- example: routing on verification status ---"
choose if source-state is equal to "verified": show "proceed with claims" otherwise show "hold or disclose"

disclose from claim-basis

remember a source called primary-source with "We evaluated four routing policies (greedy-nearest, weighted-RTT, consistent-hash, and learned-policy) across a 14-node multi-region deployment over 90 days. The learned-policy reduced p99 tail latency by 38.4% relative to greedy-nearest at the cost of a 12% increase in median CPU on routing nodes. Cache hit rates improved from 71.2% (greedy-nearest baseline) to 83.6% (learned-policy). Failover-recovery time was unchanged across all four policies (median 1.7s, p99 4.2s). The study was funded by the Edge Systems Consortium grant ESC-2024-31 and the dataset is published under CC-BY at edge-cache-data.org/halverson-roy-2025."

remember a claim called working-claim with "learned-policy reduced p99 tail latency by 38.4% relative to greedy-nearest"

remember a string called source-state with "verified"
remember a string called claim-basis with "verified"
remember a list called tracked-decisions with "none"
remember a list called open-questions with "none"
remember a number called decision-count with 0

remember how to disclose from status: show status
remember how to summarize from label: count label

cite "38.4%" from primary-source
cite "12% increase in median CPU" from primary-source
cite "71.2%" from primary-source
cite "83.6%" from primary-source
cite "median 1.7s, p99 4.2s" from primary-source
cite "14-node multi-region deployment over 90 days" from primary-source

add "finding-p99-latency-reduction-38.4pct-learned-vs-greedy" to tracked-decisions
add "finding-cpu-cost-12pct-increase-on-routing-nodes" to tracked-decisions
add "finding-cache-hit-rate-71.2pct-to-83.6pct" to tracked-decisions
add "finding-failover-recovery-unchanged-1.7s-median-4.2s-p99" to tracked-decisions

add "question-weighted-RTT-and-consistent-hash-individual-results-not-reported" to open-questions
add "question-learned-policy-architecture-not-described-in-abstract" to open-questions
add "question-whether-CPU-cost-varies-by-region-or-load" to open-questions

when source-state is equal to "verified"
  show "OK: claims grounded in verified source"

when claim-basis is equal to "verified"
  show "OK: claims grounded in verified source"

show "--- state snapshot ---"
show source-state
show claim-basis
show tracked-decisions
show open-questions

choose if source-state is equal to "verified": show "proceed with claims" otherwise show "hold or disclose"

disclose from claim-basis

add "decision-hypothesis-partially-falsified-cpu-cost-routing-node-scoped-not-fleet-wide-p99-gain-confirmed-38.4pct-cache-offset-partially-mitigates" to tracked-decisions
add "question-net-fleet-CPU-impact-not-reported-routing-node-cost-may-be-small-fraction" to open-questions
add "question-weighted-RTT-consistent-hash-results-needed-to-assess-whether-simpler-policy-closes-gap" to open-questions